@verbs spells magic cast spheres schools
@tier player
@title the spells you know and how to cast them
@see skills

Only the magic guilds teach spells; if you do not belong to one,
these four verbs have nothing to tell you.

  spells                     lists the ones you know.
  cast <spell> [<target>]    casts one.

Depending on the spell, it is cast in one of these ways:

  cast <spell>                    on yourself, on everybody or on
                                  the place (area and detection).
  cast <spell> <who>              on one creature.
  cast <spell> <a>, <b> and <c>   on several, the ones that allow it.
  cast <spell> <item>             on something you carry or that is
                                  in the place.
  cast <spell> <item> of <who>    on something somebody else wields
                                  or carries (only some spells).

Some spells need ingredients: you must carry them, and they are used
up only if the spell works. Some are required; others are optional,
and of those one of each kind you carry is used. The help of each
spell (help <spell>) says how it is cast and what it needs.

Casting takes time: there is a round of preparation, and you cannot
start another one until the first has finished. You cannot cast
while dead either, nor wearing armour your guild does not allow.

  spheres     the spheres your guild gave you, if it is clerical.
  schools     the schools, if your guild is a mage guild.

A guild uses one of the two, not both: the other verb answers that
you do not need it.
